      "answer": "$p=2$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$x^4$ term from $(px+3)^5$ is $15p^4x^4$ — B1; not $15(px)^4$.\nIdentify the term involving $6(x^3)^2(p/x)^2$ as the relevant term from the fourth power — M1.\nObtain $6p^2x^4$ for that term, hence contribution $-6p^2x^4$ in the stated difference — A1.\nSolve $15p^4-6p^2-216=0$ as a quadratic in $p^2$ — M1.\nHence $p=2$ only — B1; no other solutions.\nTotal: 5",
